  "general_identity": "For every deterministic summary T(X), P_d(A|T=t) equals sum_{x:T(x)=t} P_d(x) P(A|x) / P_d(T=t). Hence the ECL source-target residual exactly equals the direct calibration gap. Canonical uses T=S and vector A=Y; class-wise uses T=S_k and A={Y_k=1}; top-label uses T=max(S) and A={Y=argmax(S)}.",
  "method": "exact rational finite-distribution certificates plus general total-probability derivation",
